  "identifier": "nct-crc-he-100k",
  "name": "NCT-CRC-HE-100K",
  "description": "100,000 colour-normalised H&E image patches (224×224 px, 0.5 µm/px) from colorectal cancer and normal colon tissue across 9 tissue classes: adipose, background, debris, lymphocytes, mucus, smooth muscle, normal mucosa, cancer-associated stroma, and colorectal adenocarcinoma epithelium. Extracted from 86 tissue slides from NCT Cancer Center Heidelberg and University Medical Center Mannheim. Includes a 7,180-patch validation set (CRC-VAL-HE-7K). The standard benchmark for colorectal tissue classification. CC-BY-4.0, 11.7 GB, hosted on Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.1214456).",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/record/1214456",
  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
  "keywords": [
    "digital-pathology",
    "colorectal-cancer",
    "tissue-classification",
    "patch-classification",
    "h-and-e",
    "benchmark",
    "colour-normalisation",
    "adenocarcinoma",
    "zenodo"
  ],
